IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fhog-grant`

-- First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as
-- parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"); a question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The Act has one natural seat: the first home buyer, who applies for the grant (s 15), owns or will own the home
-- (s 16), must live in it (s 13), must give notice and repay if the cap or the residence requirement fails (ss 18(3),
-- 21(2)), may be required to repay (s 51), may object and seek review (ss 28, 31), and commits an offence by false
-- information (s 47). A spouse or de facto partner matters only as part of the buyer's own eligibility (ss 3, 7, 11, 12);
-- a partner who also owns the home is an applicant (s 16) and asks as a buyer. The Act puts no duty on a seller or
-- builder. The Commissioner of State Revenue and the State Administrative Tribunal are never a seat: what they may do
-- appears as what it means for the buyer. So `Role` has the one value, as every Act's layer has the same shape.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). A question that arises only in a situation takes that
-- situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it is FALSE, without reading
-- anything else. The questions of one situation share one input with the same name, type and @desc. There are four:
--   - `a grant has been paid on my application` (BOOLEAN): the eight questions of paying it back -- the s 18(3) and
--     s 21(2) duties to notify and repay and their 30 days, a required repayment (s 51(1)) and its 28 days (s 51(4)),
--     the most penalty, the interest under an arrangement (s 52, r 8(3)) and the charge on the home (s 55). Each of
--     these sections speaks of a grant paid. FALSE: does not arise;
--   - `I have a spouse or a partner I live with` (BOOLEAN): whether that person is my spouse or de facto partner for
--     the Act (ss 3, 7). FALSE: does not arise;
--   - `I have been given notice of a decision on my application` (BOOLEAN): the 60 days to object (s 28(1)(a)), which
--     run from the notice. FALSE: does not arise;
--   - `my objection has been decided` (BOOLEAN): the 60 days to apply to the State Administrative Tribunal (s 31(2)),
--     which run from notice of the objection decision. FALSE: does not arise.
-- The eligibility, cap, amount and application questions, and the fine (s 47), arise for every buyer and take none.
--
-- The rules are in fhog-grant.l4. This module calls them and restates none: each answer is the baseline export's own
-- answer, wrapped in this layer's answer types. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Months` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `months` HAS `the number of months` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `days` HAS `the number of days` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Rate` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `per cent a year` HAS `the rate` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

§§ `For the first home buyer`

§§§ `ss 3, 7, 9A-13B -- the eligibility criteria`

@export Is this person my spouse or de facto partner for the first home owner grant (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) ss 3, 7)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have a spouse or a partner I live with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the commencement date of the transaction, you are married or live with someone as a couple
      `the person` IS A Partner @desc The person, and how you live together on the commencement date of the transaction
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does this person count as my spouse or de facto partner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `I have a spouse or a partner I live with`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Is this person my spouse or de facto partner` `the person`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I old enough for the first home owner grant (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 9A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You: your history, any spouse or de facto partner, when you moved in and how long you lived there, and any period the Commissioner approved
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I old enough for the grant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Am I old enough` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do I meet the citizenship or permanent residence criterion (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) ss 7B, 10)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You: your history, any spouse or de facto partner, when you moved in and how long you lived there, and any period the Commissioner approved
      `the application` IS AN Application @desc Your application: every applicant on it, and the transaction
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I meet the citizenship or permanent residence criterion` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Do I meet the citizenship or residency criterion` `me` `the application`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I free of the bar on a second grant (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You: your history, any spouse or de facto partner, when you moved in and how long you lived there, and any period the Commissioner approved
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I free of the bar on a second grant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Am I free of the second grant bar` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I a first home owner -- have neither I nor my spouse or de facto partner held a home that counts (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 12)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You: your history, any spouse or de facto partner, when you moved in and how long you lived there, and any period the Commissioner approved
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I a first home owner for the grant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Have I never owned a home that counts` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do I meet the residence requirements -- moving in within the takeup period and living there long enough (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 13)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You: your history, any spouse or de facto partner, when you moved in and how long you lived there, and any period the Commissioner approved
      `the application` IS AN Application @desc Your application: every applicant on it, and the transaction
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I meet the residence requirements for the grant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Do I meet the residence requirements` `me` `the application`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many months must I live in the home as my principal place of residence (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 13(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You: your history, any spouse or de facto partner, when you moved in and how long you lived there, and any period the Commissioner approved
GIVETH A `Months`
`How many months must I live in my first home` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN `months` (`my required residence months` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many months after completion must I move in (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 13(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You: your history, any spouse or de facto partner, when you moved in and how long you lived there, and any period the Commissioner approved
GIVETH A `Months`
`Within how many months after completion must I move into my first home` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN `months` (`my takeup months` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I eligible for the first home owner grant -- do I meet every criterion in Part 2 Division 2 (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) ss 9-13B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You: your history, any spouse or de facto partner, when you moved in and how long you lived there, and any period the Commissioner approved
      `the application` IS AN Application @desc Your application: every applicant on it, and the transaction
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I eligible for the first home owner grant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Am I eligible` `me` `the application`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 14-14AD -- the transaction and the cap`

@export What is the cap amount -- the highest total value my home can have and still attract the grant (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 14AD; Regulations r 6)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the transaction` IS A Transaction @desc Your purchase, building contract or owner build, as it now stands
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the cap amount on my home` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN amount (`What is the cap amount for my home` `the transaction`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the total value of my transaction, which is tested against the cap (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 14AC)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the transaction` IS A Transaction @desc Your purchase, building contract or owner build, as it now stands
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What total value of my transaction is tested against the cap` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN amount (`What is the total value of my transaction` `the transaction`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my purchase or building contract an eligible transaction (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 14)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the transaction` IS A Transaction @desc Your purchase, building contract or owner build, as it now stands
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my purchase or building contract an eligible transaction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Is my transaction eligible` `the transaction`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 8, 15, 19 -- entitlement, the amount, and when to apply`

@export Is the first home owner grant payable on my application (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the application` IS AN Application @desc Your application: every applicant on it, and the transaction
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the first home owner grant payable on my application` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Is the grant payable to me` `the application`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much is my first home owner grant, if it is payable (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 19)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the transaction` IS A Transaction @desc Your purchase, building contract or owner build, as it now stands
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much is my first home owner grant, if it is payable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN amount (`How much is my grant` `the transaction`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much first home owner grant will I actually be paid on my application (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) ss 8, 19)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the application` IS AN Application @desc Your application: every applicant on it, and the transaction
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much first home owner grant will I actually be paid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN amount (`How much grant will I be paid` `the application`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Up to how many months after completion may I apply for the grant (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 15(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Months`
`Up to how many months after completion may I apply for the grant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN `months` `Up to how many months after completion may I apply`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my application in time (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 15(5), (6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `months after completion` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months after completion you apply (0 or less if before completion)
      `applied before the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied before the contract was made or the foundations began
      `the Commissioner allowed an early application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner allowed you to apply early
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my application for the grant in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Is my application in time` `months after completion` `applied before the commencement date` `the Commissioner allowed an early application`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 18, 21, 51, 52, 55 -- when I must pay it back`

@export Was I paid early and must I now give notice and repay because the total value is over the cap (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 18(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a grant has been paid on my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a first home owner grant has been paid to you, or to you and the other applicants, on this application
      `paid before completion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid to you before the transaction was completed
      `the transaction` IS A Transaction @desc Your purchase, building contract or owner build, as it now stands
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I give notice and repay because my home is over the cap` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `a grant has been paid on my application`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must I repay because my home is over the cap` `paid before completion` `the transaction`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I give notice and repay the grant because I did not move in or stay long enough (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 21(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a grant has been paid on my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a first home owner grant has been paid to you, or to you and the other applicants, on this application
      `paid in anticipation of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid to you before you had lived in the home for the required period
      `me` IS AN Applicant @desc You: your history, any spouse or de facto partner, when you moved in and how long you lived there, and any period the Commissioner approved
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I give notice and repay because I did not move in or stay long enough` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `a grant has been paid on my application`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must I repay because of residence` `paid in anticipation of residence` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many days must I give notice and repay, or apply for an arrangement (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) ss 18(3), 21(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a grant has been paid on my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a first home owner grant has been paid to you, or to you and the other applicants, on this application
GIVETH A `Days`
`Within how many days must I give notice and repay the grant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `a grant has been paid on my application`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` `Within how many days must I notify and repay`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Commissioner make me repay the grant (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 51(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a grant has been paid on my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a first home owner grant has been paid to you, or to you and the other applicants, on this application
      `paid in error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid in error
      `the Commissioner reversed the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner reversed the decision to pay
      `I failed to meet a condition of the grant in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to meet a condition of the grant within its period
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Commissioner make me repay the grant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `a grant has been paid on my application`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I be made to repay` `paid in error` `the Commissioner reversed the decision` `I failed to meet a condition of the grant in time`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many days of the notice must I pay a required repayment or penalty (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 51(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a grant has been paid on my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a first home owner grant has been paid to you, or to you and the other applicants, on this application
GIVETH A `Days`
`Within how many days of the notice must I pay a required repayment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `a grant has been paid on my application`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` `Within how many days of notice must I repay`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most penalty I can be charged on top of the amount I must repay (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) ss 18(6), 21(5a), 51(2), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a grant has been paid on my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a first home owner grant has been paid to you, or to you and the other applicants, on this application
      `the amount I must repay` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of grant you are required to repay, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most penalty I can be charged on top of the repayment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `a grant has been paid on my application`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`What is the most penalty I can be charged` `the amount I must repay`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What interest rate, per cent a year, applies to an arrangement to repay later or by instalments (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 52(3)(a); Regulations r 8(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a grant has been paid on my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a first home owner grant has been paid to you, or to you and the other applicants, on this application
GIVETH A `Rate`
`What interest rate applies to an arrangement to repay the grant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `a grant has been paid on my application`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `per cent a year` `What interest rate applies to my repayment arrangement`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the Commissioner register a charge over my home for the grant (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 55)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a grant has been paid on my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a first home owner grant has been paid to you, or to you and the other applicants, on this application
      `I owe a repayment, penalty or costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you owe a repayment, penalty, arrangement amount or costs under the Act
      `I still own the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you still hold the relevant interest in the home
      `paid in anticipation of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the grant was paid to you before you had lived in the home for the required period
      `the Commissioner believes I mean to sell before meeting the residence requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner reasonably believes you intend to sell before meeting them
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the Commissioner register a charge over my home` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `a grant has been paid on my application`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can a charge be put on my home` `I owe a repayment, penalty or costs` `I still own the home` `paid in anticipation of residence` `the Commissioner believes I mean to sell before meeting the residence requirements`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 22, 28, 31, 47 -- offences, objection and review`

@export What is the most I can be fined for giving false or misleading information, or breaking a grant condition (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) ss 22(4), 47)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined under the grant Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN amount `What is the most I can be fined`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many days of notice of the decision must I object (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 28(1)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been given notice of a decision on my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has given you notice of a decision on your application or about the grant
GIVETH A `Days`
`Within how many days of notice of the decision must I object` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `I have been given notice of a decision on my application`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` `Within how many days must I object`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many days of the objection decision must I apply to the State Administrative Tribunal (First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA) s 31(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my objection has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lodged an objection and the Commissioner has given you notice of the decision on it
GIVETH A `Days`
`Within how many days of the objection decision must I apply for review` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN
        IF NOT `my objection has been decided`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `days` `Within how many days must I seek review`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Duties Act 2008 s 142A -- the transfer duty concession`

@export Am I a concessional first home owner for the transfer duty concession (Duties Act 2008 (WA) s 142A, read with the First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 (WA))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the application` IS AN Application @desc Your application: every applicant on it, and the transaction
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I a concessional first home owner for transfer duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying or building my first home in Western Australia` THEN `yes if` (`Am I a concessional first home owner for duty` `the application`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
